From: Gordon McNab <gordon@ayjen1.enet.dec.com>
Subject: RE: need help installing NT 3.5 on AlphaStation 400

Greg,

>This is the error message I get if I select VGA for the video. 

There is no generic VGA driver included in the Windows NT 3.51 CDROM for Alpha 
systems. You need to have the correct driver disk for the video card you intend 
to use before installing the Operating system.

>the floppy I created from the drvlib/video/cirrus/alpha directory on 
>the CD-ROM or the drivers I FTPed from gatekeeper.dec.com

Likewise, the Cirrus drivers are not compatible with the ZLXp-E1 video card. You 
can ftp another copy of the ZLXp-E1 drivers from:

http://www.windowsnt.digital.com/support/drivers/drivers.htm

Follow the instructions in the zip file and that should keep you straight. And 
as John Crookshank said, do a 'Custom Install'. 

Gordon

