Thanks to everyone who responded to my plea for help installing NT 3.5 on AlphaStation 400

Several people pointed out that:
 
> There is no generic VGA driver included in the Windows NT 3.51 CDROM for Alpha 
> systems. You need to have the correct driver disk for the video card you intend 
> to use before installing the Operating system.

As for the floppies I created from the drvlib/video/cirrus/alpha 
directory on the CD-ROM or the drivers I FTPed from 
gatekeeper.dec.com; Gordon McNab pointed out :

> the Cirrus drivers are not compatible with the ZLXp-E1 video card. You 
> can ftp another copy of the ZLXp-E1 drivers from:
> 
> http://www.windowsnt.digital.com/support/drivers/drivers.htm
> 
> Follow the instructions in the zip file and that should keep you straight

Surprise, surprise, I was able to get past my problem using another 
solution this morning. And I didn't even have to issue a purchase 
order for software or software support.

A week ago, when I checked ftp://gatekeeper.dec.com/private/fwaxp for 
new drivers, etc, there was only one file that seemed related to ZLX 
video drivers, that being  zlxv23.zip . I had downloaded that, copied 
it onto 2 diskettes as explained in the readme .... but it didn't 
work.  So this morning, I checked that same directory again, and lo 
and behold, there was a file called zlxv20.zip . I downloaded this 
and extracted it onto a single diskette, as per the readme and this 
got me past my initial problem

I've downloaded and installed a number of updates, etc, so I'm not 
sure what the proper solution would have been ... but I suspect 
downloading the zlxv20.zip file probably would have done the trick.

Thanks again.

Greg

