Date: Sat, 4 Nov 1995 14:00:24 +0200 (EET)
From: Petteri Heino <kt04793@UWasa.Fi>
Subject: Even more perf tests

I did some tests with a domestic 3D-package called Real3D. Version
2.4 to be exact. In case some wants data on the older machines, here's
some clues:

Machine	AlphaStation 400 	DECpc AXP/150	Pentium

Mhz	233			150		90
OS	NT 3.5 WS		NT 3.5 WS	Windows 3.11
Card	ZLX-p-E1		Qvision/1024E	CL5434
Bus	PCI			EISA		PCI
RAM	32 Mb			32 Mb		16 Mb

The idea was to put typical configurations to a test. The old Windows 3.11
would not speed up too much even if it had 32 megs of RAM. Generally the
tests are made so that if possible the effect of the display adapter would
not be significant.

Lower is better. Send me mail if you need more accurate info
on the tests or Real3D. Basically these are FP-intensive stuff worked out
with the assistance of Realsoft, the manufacturer:

