Apparently some users are having problems with the RZ-29B's in RAID
configurations.  I have a copy of a message posted on the Alpha-OSF
managers forum.  Here it is....  Remember I am just passing this along.  If
you want more info you will have to contact the originator.

John Nichols
Maine Yankee Atomic Power Co	
nicholsj@myapc.com	
(207) 798-4270
-----------
The RZ29B drives on RAID have shown problems that are  suppossed
to be fixed by upgrading to the version 0014  firmware.

If you are experiencing drives that are being failed by the  controller and
when pulled and put back seem to function OK,  you are probably
seeing the problem

We have identical 2100 5/250 servers with 3 channel RAID  and RZ29B
drives. One system runs VMS and the other  Digital UNIX.  We were
seeing drive failures on both systems  at least every two weeks.  The
UNIX system lost no data but  the VMS system was not so lucky.  We
run RAID 5.

We have been pursuing the issue with DEC since September  and only
last week determined that it was an identified  problem.  There are two
fixes apparently, a short term fix of  setting a bit in a mode register on
the drive or the firmware  upgrade.  

The firmware may not be officially released yet but is on the  way.

