Subject: Re: Terminal Emulation

> Can anyone put me onto some good terminal emulation software
> (preferably vt320) for Windows NT 3.51 on an AlphaStation 200?

Kermit.   The newest version (for Win95 and Windows NT) is no
longer free, but still costs under $50 from Columbia University.

The only flaw I am aware of in the emulation (and this was
in the earlier MS-DOS version) is that it does not properly
handle the selective erase (protected vs non-protected fields)
function.   I reported this problem several years ago, but
do not know if it has been fixed.   I got the impression that
it was a low-priority bug.   In fact, I have only found one
application that uses that escape sequence, and the problem
went away when I changed the emulation to VT-100.

