>package, or is a binary translator ala the DECmigrate toolset for VMS?
>
>I've heard "coming in '96" for the 386 or better emulation, to replace 
>the current 286 emulation in NT.

FX!32 is like the DECmigrate tools in that it provides direct binary 
TRANSLATION of the Win32/Intel code to Win32/Alpha.  It is NOT emulation 
software.  The "coming in '96" information you have heard is for the Intel 
emulation software which is currently included inside RISC version of NT. 
It is currently only 286 instructions.  The next release is expected to 
contain 486 instructions.  This is EMULATION software, not translation.

-Ken

