Subject: Re: Problem with ENV variables
In-Reply-To: <951115140240.204001ac@uvphys.phys.UVic.CA>

The reason why you cannot do this, is NT does not allow a environmental 
variable to hold another environmental variable. Nested env variables are 
not allowed.

%mosaic.ini% cannot have another env var within it. To prove this, type 

	ECHO %USERNAME%

	SET TEST=%USERNAME%

then

	ECHO %TEST%

You get %usename% don't you. The solution is to somehow call Mosaic (I 
don't use it and don't know the command line options) with a command line 
parameter that points to c:\users\%username%\mosaic.ini for the config file.

The alternative is to NOT have any mosaic.ini's in the Systems path and 
make a login script that will add "c:\users\%username%" to thier path... That 
way when they start the app, it will look in the path for an INI and find 
it in the users directory.

